Third-party components
----------------------

usb-serial-for-android (Android only)
  Used on Android for USB-serial chipset drivers (FTDI, CP21xx, CH34x, PL2303,
  CDC/ACM, ...). Its sources are vendored under third_party/usb-serial-for-android/
  and compiled into an embedded classes.dex at build time (loaded at runtime via
  a DexClassLoader; see docs/android.md).
  Copyright (C) 2013 Google Inc. and later contributors
  (https://github.com/kai-morich/usb-serial-for-android)
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see that directory for the
  license text (LICENSE.txt).

boost (boost::asio) (Linux/Windows only)
  Used for portable serial I/O (header-only usage; the public header includes
  <boost/asio.hpp>, so consumers need Boost headers as well).
  Distributed under the Boost Software License, Version 1.0.
